WittyBluray is an original implementation of the Blu-ray Disc (HDMV)
navigation model written from the publicly documented disc structure. It
contains no code from other players, and it does not decrypt AACS-protected
discs or run BD+. Format details were checked against public documentation and
the published source of open players, as facts; no code was copied.

bdj/runtime.jar is original code that re-implements the published interfaces
disc applications link against. It is not a Java runtime, contains no Java
runtime, and has not been tested for compatibility by any certifying body.
